{"title":"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Amanda ordered a dozen donuts. She said she wanted only chocolate, glazed, and powdered donuts, and at least one of each kind. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of chocolate, glazed, and powdered donuts she wound up with. Find the number of possible ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>She has a dozen unknown donuts: D, D, D, D, D, D, D, D, D, D, D, D. We can set dividers between the D's and come up with some chocolate, glazed, and powdered donuts using the following rules:\n</p><p>We set two dividers between the D's so that they split the D's into three groups. The left group is chocolate, the middle group is glazed, and the right group is powdered.\n</p><p>There are 11 spaces between the D's, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/2614b7249042a1565dbd265c273d5fe892dfcec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{11}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" /> ways to set the dividers. Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4ab753c667adcc751fc04a18166b375bbdc4956d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{55}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> ways to get three kinds of donuts totaling 12.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST\">2006 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<center><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 12\">A similar problem</a></center>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017084349\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 92/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1382/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 215/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1056/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.958      1 Template:ARML_box\n100.00%    6.958      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6725:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017084349 and revision id 26658. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}